# Patch 0061 — theme engine correctness: one Midnight, one light/dark authority,
# and a contrast check that actually runs.
#
# SYMPTOM (user, 2026-08-03): "every theme setting is also glitchy and buggy
# right now"; "check contrast between text and background when switching themes".
#
# Five defects, all found by reading the live tree, all measured before and after.
#
# 1. THE DEFAULT THEME TOOK A DIFFERENT CODE PATH FROM EVERY OTHER THEME.
#    applyToWindow() returned early for kavacha-midnight on the theory that
#    patch 0016's baked floor already carried its colours. The floor carried SIX
#    of eighteen. So at the shipped default --kavacha-accent,
#    --kavacha-tab-active-background, --kavacha-tab-hover-background and nine
#    more were undefined, and their consumers in kavacha-menu.inc.css and
#    kavacha-polish.inc.css fell through to `color-mix(in srgb, currentColor …)`
#    — a TEXT-derived colour standing in for a tab colour. Switch to Forest and
#    they became real colours; switch back and they became text again. Measured
#    before: 6 of 18 tokens defined at the default, 18 at every other theme.
#    After: 18 everywhere, verified for all three built-ins.
#
# 2. THERE WERE THREE DEFINITIONS OF "MIDNIGHT" AND THE WINNER WAS THE ONE
#    NOBODY EDITED. kavacha-midnight.inc.css said #14111f; BUILTIN_THEMES said
#    #14111F; kavacha-theme-fixes.inc.css (patch 0033) said #0b0912 and, being
#    %include'd last, won. 0033's values were the tuned ones, so they are now
#    the values in all three places and 0033's token block is deleted. Nothing
#    was lightened — this is a move, not a retune.
#
# 3. LIGHT THEMES WERE ONLY HALF LIGHT. The engine wrote
#    `root.style.colorScheme` inline, which reaches :root and nothing else,
#    while Zen applies color-scheme to `:root, panel, menupopup,
#    .zen-browser-generic-background, #urlbar[breakout-extend],
#    #tabbrowser-tabpanels browser[type=content]` and the toast container,
#    gated on a `zen.view.window.scheme` pref that knows nothing about Kavacha
#    themes. Kavacha Daylight therefore produced a light frame over dark popups,
#    dark menus and dark content, with --zen-urlbar-filter still on its
#    brightness(25%) dark branch: a near-black urlbar on a white browser.
#
#    A pref could not fix this and an overlay could not either. Zen's block is
#    anchored on `#main-window[windowtype='navigator:browser']:not(
#    [chromehidden~='toolbar'])` — specificity (1,2,0), which no :root-based
#    rule can outrank. The new kavacha-theme-scheme.inc.css re-uses that exact
#    anchor plus the mode attribute, putting every arm one or two attributes
#    above the arm it must beat, and %includes Zen's own schemes/*.inc.css
#    rather than copying their values. Private windows keep Zen's forced dark.
#
# 4. TWO DERIVATIONS OF LIGHT/DARK THAT COULD DISAGREE. themeMode() read the
#    theme's DECLARED surface and stamped the attribute; _applyColorScheme()
#    read the COMPUTED one. The old header claimed they could not disagree
#    because they shared a threshold — they never shared an input. Now one
#    function, one input (computed), one attribute; the CSS owns the rest.
#
#    And the colour parser accepted hex and rgb() only. hsl(), oklch(),
#    color-mix() or a named colour returned null, and null meant "dark",
#    silently — a white theme rendered as dark chrome, white on white, with no
#    console line. Colours now resolve through the style system itself, so
#    whatever CSS accepts, this accepts. Verified with a theme authored in
#    hsl() and a named colour.
#
# 5. NOTHING EVER CHECKED CONTRAST. Added, using the real WCAG formula. The
#    luminance the old code used skipped sRGB gamma linearisation, which is
#    serviceable for a light/dark guess and wrong for a ratio. Every apply now
#    measures text-on-surface and, below 4.5:1, substitutes readable text rather
#    than shipping chrome you cannot read; contrastOf() exposes the verdict so
#    patch 0063 can badge the theme. A theme package is arbitrary marketplace
#    data and nothing stopped it from leaving the browser with no legible UI.
#
# Also fixed here, being one-line consequences of the same audit:
#   * applyToWindow tore down BEFORE resolving, so a corrupt package stripped
#     the current theme and installed nothing, on every window open.
#   * applyToAllWindows never awaited, so a slow on-disk theme could land its
#     writes on top of a faster switch — pref, Settings and Studio all saying
#     one theme while the chrome wore another. Generation counter added.
#   * _managedProps was one process-wide Set used to tear down PER-WINDOW
#     inline styles. Now a WeakMap, like _sheetByWindow already was.
#   * --kavacha-horizontal-strip-height was read with fallback 44px in one place
#     and 42px in another and defined nowhere, so the tab wrapper sat
#     permanently 2px short of its own row. Defined once.
#
# NEW BEHAVIOUR: light/dark becomes a user choice. kavacha.theme.follow-system
# plus kavacha.theme.active-dark / -light remember a pick per side.
# kavacha.theme.active remains the single authority for what is applied, so the
# Studio, the Settings pane and the marketplace are untouched.
#
# WHY NOT A PREF OR AN OVERLAY: the token floor is a build-time %include and the
# engine is a system module; neither is reachable from ui/ or customization/.
# The specificity problem in (3) is structural — see above.
#
# VERIFIED (Marionette, 758px window, buildID 20260803):
#   * 18/18 tokens defined under Midnight, Forest and Daylight; none missing.
#   * Daylight -> color-scheme "light" on :root, panel, menupopup AND
#     browser[type=content]; --zen-urlbar-filter on brightness(75%). Forcing
#     zen.view.window.scheme to 0 (dark) changes none of them.
#   * Contrast, built-ins: 18.14 / 16.40 / 16.01 primary, all pass.
#   * A grey-on-grey theme authored in hsl() + a named colour: 1.37:1 as
#     authored, repaired to 4.61 primary / 4.92 secondary on apply.
#   * Midnight -> Forest -> Midnight: all 18 tokens byte-identical.
#
# FILES: src/zen/common/sys/KavachaThemeEngine.sys.mjs;
# src/zen/kavacha-theme/kavacha-midnight.inc.css;
# src/zen/common/styles/kavacha-theme-fixes.inc.css;
# src/zen/common/styles/kavacha-theme-scheme.inc.css (new);
# src/zen/common/styles/zen-theme.css.
# Also mirrored outside the patch series, in the repo proper:
# customization/themes/kavacha-midnight/colors.json.
