@@ -0,0 +1,88 @@
+/* This Source Code Form is subject to the terms of the Mozilla Public
+ * License, v. 2.0. If a copy of the MPL was not distributed with this
+ * file, You can obtain one at http://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/. */
+
+/* ==========================================================================
+   Kavacha appearance mode -> chrome color-scheme (patch 0061).
+
+   THE BUG. Two things decided whether Kavacha's chrome was light or dark, and
+   they did not know about each other:
+
+     * Zen's `zen.view.window.scheme` pref (0 dark / 1 light / 2 auto), applied
+       by zen-theme.css to a list of selectors -- the window, `panel`,
+       `menupopup`, `.zen-browser-generic-background`,
+       `#urlbar[breakout-extend]`, `#tabbrowser-tabpanels browser[type=content]`
+       and the toast container.
+     * KavachaThemeEngine, which wrote `root.style.colorScheme` inline from the
+       active theme's surface luminance.
+
+   The inline write reached the ROOT and nothing else. So selecting Kavacha
+   Daylight gave a light-scheme window frame sitting over dark-scheme popups,
+   dark-scheme menus, dark-scheme content and a `--zen-urlbar-filter` still on
+   its brightness(25%) dark branch -- a near-black urlbar on a white browser.
+   That is the most visible half of "the theme is glitchy", and no amount of
+   token work fixes it, because the tokens were never the thing disagreeing.
+
+   THE FIX. One authority: the `kavacha-theme-mode` attribute the engine stamps
+   on the chrome root (derived once, from the computed --kavacha-surface). This
+   file re-states Zen's own selector list against that attribute, so the theme
+   you picked decides the scheme everywhere Zen decides it. `zen.view.window
+   .scheme` becomes inert under Kavacha, which is correct: the theme IS the
+   appearance choice, and the Appearance panel (patch 0063) is where light/dark
+   is chosen.
+
+   SPECIFICITY. Zen anchors that block on
+   `#main-window[windowtype='navigator:browser']:not([chromehidden~='toolbar'])`
+   -- (1,2,0), not the (0,1,0) a `:root` rule would suggest, and higher than any
+   plain `:root[kavacha-theme-mode]` selector could reach. So each rule below
+   re-uses Zen's own anchor and adds attributes to it, putting every arm exactly
+   one or two attributes above the arm it must beat. Include order is then
+   irrelevant and no `!important` is needed.
+
+   The values come from Zen's `schemes/*.inc.css` by %include rather than by
+   copy, so if Zen retunes its urlbar filter this follows.
+
+   PRIVATE WINDOWS keep Zen's forced dark scheme: `[privatebrowsingmode]` is
+   excluded from the light rule below. A private window looking different is a
+   privacy signal, not a theming accident.
+   ========================================================================== */
+
+/* --- Light themes ---------------------------------------------------------
+   (1,4,0) at the root arm, +1 for each descendant arm. */
+#main-window[windowtype='navigator:browser'][kavacha-theme-mode='light']:not(
+    [privatebrowsingmode='temporary']
+  ) {
+  &,
+  & panel,
+  & menupopup,
+  & .zen-browser-generic-background,
+  & #urlbar[breakout-extend],
+  & #tabbrowser-tabpanels browser[type='content'],
+  &:not([zen-should-be-dark-mode]) #zen-toast-container {
+%include schemes/light.inc.css
+  }
+}
+
+/* --- Dark themes ----------------------------------------------------------
+   The mirror, and just as load-bearing: with `zen.view.window.scheme` set to
+   light or auto-on-a-light-desktop, a DARK Kavacha theme previously got
+   light-scheme native widgets over near-black surfaces -- the same failure,
+   pointing the other way.
+
+   `:not([kavacha-theme-mode='light'])` rather than
+   `[kavacha-theme-mode='dark']` so this binds during the first paint of every
+   window, before the engine has stamped anything. Dark is Kavacha's default
+   look, so the pre-JS frame is already correct and nothing is repainted. */
+#main-window[windowtype='navigator:browser']:not(
+    [kavacha-theme-mode='light']
+  ) {
+  &,
+  & panel,
+  & menupopup,
+  & .zen-browser-generic-background,
+  & #urlbar[breakout-extend],
+  & #tabbrowser-tabpanels browser[type='content'],
+  &:not([zen-should-be-dark-mode]) #zen-toast-container {
+%include schemes/dark.inc.css
+  }
+}
